            <div xml:id="d22">

                <pb facs="0135" n="37" xml:id="pg37"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/11195: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-09-16T22:00:00+08:00">September 16, 1930—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 16—1:16 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>818. Following telegram has been sent to American Consul General at Shanghai:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“September 16, 9 p.m. [Paraphrase.] Today Quo Tai-chi<anchor n="33"
                                xml:id="d22-f1"/> called to say that it was very likely Mr. Tong
                                Shao-yi<anchor n="34" xml:id="d22-f2"/> would approach you in order
                            to transmit to the Legation a message for Wang Ching-wei. I pointed out,
                            in reply, the possible impropriety if complying with such a request
                            involved American officials in transmitting a message having a political
                            character. It would appear advisable not to accept any message for
                            transmission pending approval by the Department. Repeated to the
                            Department. [End paraphrase.]”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d22-f1" n="33" xml:id="d22-f1-content">
                <p>Representative of Wang Ching-wei.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d22-f2" n="34" xml:id="d22-f2-content">
                <p>Veteran member of the Kuomintang.</p>
